# @code/gleam — the Gleam altitude grammar.
#
# Gleam's instance of @code. Same family as @code/rust (D2;
# shards/code/rust.mirror) and @code/mirror (shards/code/mirror.mirror);
# each declares the five operations on its own source manifold under
# the universal @code discipline (shards/code.mirror).
#
# Migrated from boot/04b-code-gleam.mirror (the legacy boot kernel
# form) with the same substrate-pull tightenings as @code/rust:
#
#   - no LSP-action stubs in the altitude declaration. The previous
#     boot kernel form declared `action complete(position) in @code/gleam
#     { }` etc.; per the substrate-pull pattern crystallized at
#     @code/rust, the altitude grammar declares the five-op block and
#     altitude-specific shape, NOT the LSP-action surface. LSP actions
#     belong to a separate seam (boot/04-code's `abstract action`
#     declarations name the universal LSP surface; consumers wire them
#     against altitudes at the transport layer, not in the altitude
#     grammar itself).
#
#   - no Gleam type fragments at this floor. The previous form declared
#     `type int`, `type float`, `type bit_array`, etc. directly in the
#     altitude grammar. Per the @code/rust precedent, primitive type
#     declarations belong to the altitude's source-language model
#     downstream (a future @code/gleam/types sub-prism, or the
#     compiler's symbol-table layer), not to the altitude root. The
#     altitude root declares the five-op prism shape; specializations
#     compose under it.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-triple-binary.md §3 (the translate
# template family); roadmap/wip/butterfly-self-hosting.md (gleam is
# named in Mara/Reed's substrate plans as a future @code family member
# but is not yet a Phase-D target — this shard exists as the
# substrate-pull-realize migration of the boot kernel declaration, not
# as a Phase-D commitment).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: code.mirror (the universal parent),
#                 code/rust.mirror (D2; the precedent instance),
#                 code/mirror.mirror (sibling instance).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/gleam.mirror`
# declares `@code/gleam` and only that.

out @code/gleam
